<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31794" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκγελάω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξεγέλασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					389
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				4.37
			</span></i> :—<i>laugh out, laugh loud,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδὺ δ᾽ ἄρ᾽ ἐκγελάσας μετεφώνεε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.354
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				18.35
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.3.9
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέλωτι ὥσπερ κῦμα ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					473c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐάν τις κνήσῃ, ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					965a24
				</span></i>
			 : metaph. of a liquid that rushes out with a
			<i>gurgling</i> sound, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκγελᾷ φόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1176
				</span></i>
			.</div>
